18
00:00:29,562 --> 00:00:30,475
Now add the government.

19
00:00:30,900 --> 00:00:32,812
The United States keeps running deficits,

20
00:00:33,050 --> 00:00:34,375
so it keeps borrowing too.

21
00:00:34,800 --> 00:00:37,488
Cuban says the country is already paying around

22
00:00:37,500 --> 00:00:39,600
a trillion dollars a year in interest.

23
00:00:40,012 --> 00:00:42,138
And when the government and the AI giants

24
00:00:42,150 --> 00:00:44,388
are all competing for the same lenders,

25
00:00:44,738 --> 00:00:45,863
interest rates go up.

26
00:00:46,288 --> 00:00:47,225
His math is simple.

27
00:00:47,638 --> 00:00:49,888
If you owe forty billion dollars and rates

28
00:00:49,900 --> 00:00:50,637
keep climbing,

29
00:00:51,012 --> 00:00:52,975
at some point you can't raise money anymore.

30
00:00:53,388 --> 00:00:54,425
Something gets crowded out.

31
00:00:54,850 --> 00:00:55,288
Which thing?

32
00:00:55,725 --> 00:00:57,613
He admits he's not enough of a financial

33
00:00:57,625 --> 00:00:58,388
expert to say.

34
00:00:58,812 --> 00:01:00,175
But something, he says,

35
00:01:00,388 --> 00:01:01,075
is going to give.

36
00:01:01,500 --> 00:01:03,038
That's why he once joked that a lot

37
00:01:03,050 --> 00:01:05,125
of today's data centers will end up as

38
00:01:05,138 --> 00:01:06,175
pickleball courts.

39
00:01:06,588 --> 00:01:07,300
It's a metaphor,

40
00:01:07,575 --> 00:01:09,025
not a forecast about sport.

41
00:01:09,450 --> 00:01:11,662
His point is that real progress in AI

42
00:01:11,675 --> 00:01:13,363
should mean less power doing more.

43
00:01:13,775 --> 00:01:16,325
Right now, the industry does more by burning

44
00:01:16,338 --> 00:01:16,712
more.

45
00:01:17,162 --> 00:01:17,900
Here's the twist.

46
00:01:18,312 --> 00:01:20,250
You might expect this from an AI skeptic.

47
00:01:20,662 --> 00:01:22,775
Instead, it comes from the man who built

48
00:01:22,838 --> 00:01:24,062
Broadcast dot com,

49
00:01:24,438 --> 00:01:26,488
back when people told him streaming was a

50
00:01:26,500 --> 00:01:26,925
joke.

51
00:01:27,338 --> 00:01:29,600
So does Cuban think AI is overhyped?

52
00:01:30,012 --> 00:01:30,700
Not exactly.

53
00:01:31,125 --> 00:01:32,350
He thinks it's misunderstood.
